description.narrative:
The results achieved include the following:
1. During Sept 2018 - December 2019, there has been the following visits between Swedish Tax Agency (STA) and State Fiscal Service of Ukraine (SFS):
- STA visit to Kyiv, Ukraine on 10-14 September, 2018;
- SFS visit to Stockholm, Sweden 4-10 November 2018;
- STA visit to Kyiv, Ukraine 14-18 January 2019;
- STA visit to Kyiv, Ukraine 22-26 July, 2019;
2.  STA submitted the first draft proposal in May 2019 (the deadline was 31 January 2019) but received Embassy's comments for substantial improvement in terms of substance (create Workplan, Risk matrix, Results matrix, Budget with units and cost per unit etc). STA asked for cost extension to do the additionall work on proposal, and the Embassy granted the cost extension of SEK 1.2 million. The second more elaborate draft proposal was submitted in December 2020. After this, there has been still continuous dialogue on further proposal improvement in terms of mainstreaming Sida development perspective and anti-corruption, and budget structure set up that would allow a clear budget follow up etc. The last draft proposal with all annexes was submitted on 25 May 2020 even with the activity period for the new 3-year contribution (Plan-it 12787) started 1 January 2020.
In addition to the above cost extension, the Embassy also made 2 no-cost agreement amendments to:
1) extend the activity period from 31 January 2019 to 1 September 2019, and
2) approve the reallocation between fees and reimbursables of SEK 54 309.81 as requested in by STA.
The Embassy's experience is that the preparation of the project required quite a lot of efforts and time from the Embassy side to bring the proposal to the Sida standards, as well as manage administratively the agreement no-cost and cost extensions.
